{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/410140-in-which-dark-age-books-do-i-find-a-chart-on-faith-rating-per-holy-building","id":410140,"title":"in which dark age books do i find a chart on faith rating per holy building?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-18T09:00:37-08:00","id":410140,"title":"in which dark age books do i find a chart on faith rating per holy building?","content":"i think there was one but i can't remember..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T12:13:27-08:00","id":410422,"title":"","content":"Jerusalem by Night, if memory serves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T10:37:09-08:00","id":411748,"title":"","content":"There are True Faith ratings for the major religious buildings in DA Jerusalem in the Mage part of Darkening Skies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T10:52:40-08:00","id":411777,"title":"","content":"Also see page 122 of the Dark Ages companion for a list of what effect faith ratings have on vampires, disciplines etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T09:45:18-08:00","id":412896,"title":"","content":"There's also a nice bit about how True Faith affects the magic of various Fellowships in the same section of Darkening Skies. <br /> <br /> It's a pretty good thing to be in the Messianic Voices. Not so bad in a lot of places for Ahl-i-Batin. Not so good for Old Faith or Valdermen....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T05:48:44-08:00","id":418632,"title":"","content":"i don;t see why old faith and valderment can't have their own true faith.<br /> <br /> true faith isn'tthe dominion of ars magica. hell,i could,in theory ward against vampires by using a credid card because of my belief in money<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T08:53:22-08:00","id":418792,"title":"","content":"Why do you bring Ars Magica in this? It's totally irrelevent to the discussion.<br /> <br /> Old Faith and Valderman doesn't have True Faith as its mechanic is tied to Abrahamic Religions (Judaism, Islam and Christianity) and how they perceived Faith and the relationship of man and God. So obviously non-pious people (like most polytheists who saw God just as one more person to pray to IF NEEDED) would have no True Faith rating and &quot;suffer&quot; in a Holy Place as they would be out of tune.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T08:53:32-08:00","id":418793,"title":"","content":"The True Faith you are going to find in Jerusalem, isn't going to pose that question. <br /> <br /> In the cemetery outside Uppsala, you can start worrying about whether there's True Faith in DA for Valderman. In a major henge or at a sacred well, ditto for Old Faith. But True Faith doesn't have to be equal opportunity. Otherwise you are going to have to start figuring out where the Order of Hermes has ITS True Faith venues. And that just... doesn't seem right....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T12:12:32-08:00","id":419121,"title":"","content":"i merely mentioned ars magica as an example of a game where the monotheistic abrahamic religions are special by canon.<br /> <br /> as for the order of hermes.. i think it depends. it's certainly not inconcivable that some christian magus from ex miscelanea may have a paradigm that matches the true faith of the church of the holy sepulchre.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T13:18:32-08:00","id":419252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/410140-in-which-dark-age-books-do-i-find-a-chart-on-faith-rating-per-holy-building?p=418792#post418792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you bring Ars Magica in this? It's totally irrelevent to the discussion.<br /> <br /> Old Faith and Valderman doesn't have True Faith as its mechanic is tied to Abrahamic Religions (Judaism, Islam and Christianity) and how they perceived Faith and the relationship of man and God. So obviously non-pious people (like most polytheists who saw God just as one more person to pray to IF NEEDED) would have no True Faith rating and &quot;suffer&quot; in a Holy Place as they would be out of tune.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that V20 has the Baali weakness be an aversion to <i>any</i> holy symbols, rather than the cross specifically, I'm really doubting that True Faith is tied to any particular belief. It's more about strength of faith than what that faith is in. I also think that Hunters Hunted 2 says something about this very subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T13:31:44-08:00","id":419270,"title":"","content":"perhaps true faith is more common among the abrahamic faiths because they have(relatively speaking) and more rigid belief system.<br /> <br /> im no religion expert but if im not mistakes there's no bible-quran equivelant to be found in ancient greek religion for example. during the times of rome for instance<br /> <br /> most people had no problem with the belief that some gods were the same interpreted in a different way. <br /> <br /> besides whenyour pantheon has 20+ members adding a few more doesn't hurt.<br /> <br /> <br /> though if my hypothesis is true it has some unfortunate implications.<br /> it may mean that in the cwod your average gay-loving liberal church focusing on jesus love would be vampire chew food.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> while turning gay bashing into a phiosophy would drastically improve your lifespan","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T14:20:10-08:00","id":419313,"title":"","content":"If that's the metric we're using for True Faith, than no modern Christian stands a chance; eating shellfish, wearing mixed cloth, and working on Sundays apparently means their faith is meaningless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T16:04:42-08:00","id":419494,"title":"","content":"I can't remeber right now, but I'm absolutely sure that in some DA sourcebook there was either a side-bar or several paragraphs on the topic of non-Monotheistic True Faith (Road of Haven, maybe? Can't remember, really).<br /> <br /> The thing is - yes, there could be a &quot;pagan&quot; with True Faith. But. given the state of things in DA setting they are less numerous then their monotheistic counterparts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","name":"von Lyttenburgh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3479_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T17:46:01-08:00","id":419632,"title":"","content":"True Faith has absolutely nothing to do with religion and everything to do with Faith. The reason Christianity and Islam are so highly featured in the DA line is because they are the predominant religions of the era, and the majority of the people in the area covered by the game will be of those Faiths, therfore most Saints will actually come from those faiths.<br /> <br /> Other then that... True Faith comes from within. From a singular perception of the World and ones place in itself. There is no difference if you believe in Buddha, Jesus, Mohammed, Solomon or Athena - as long as you are just and faithful you are golden. Remember that Faith is personal and that religion is an external political construct.<br /> <br /> So, Yes. You could be a Gay Muslim or a Heretic Christian and still have True Faith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T00:47:13-08:00","id":419949,"title":"","content":"Asmodai has it right. There is also True Faith for the Infernal, can be found for example in Infernalism: Path of Screams, as it is not tied to any particular religion but like said in to individuals own faith. Christianity just has more True Faith wielding members in the DA setting because they have greater numbers in general and so a better chance of attracting those who are willing to devote themselves wholly to their faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T08:39:49-08:00","id":420262,"title":"","content":"just in case anyone else is interested hagia sophia from bitter crusade has(back then at least) a faith rating of 8. <br /> <br /> likewise i think areas like <br /> <br /> Masjid_al-Haram would propable have 8 as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T09:56:49-08:00","id":420392,"title":"","content":"If the Hagia Sophia has a TF rating of 8, Jerusalem should be scattered with 9's with a few 10's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T09:59:48-08:00","id":420399,"title":"","content":"Given that pretty much anything can constitute a basis for True Faith, doesn't that render it effectively meaningless?<br /> <br /> Ex. (NOT REAL) I REALLY believe in the color pink. It colors (literally) everything I see (rose-colored glasses and all), what I do, where I go, what I wear, how I think about things. Any subject you bring up I can come up with some way it's impacted by pink and how it can be made better by pink... Vampires beware.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T13:29:10-08:00","id":420582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/410140-in-which-dark-age-books-do-i-find-a-chart-on-faith-rating-per-holy-building?p=420392#post420392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Hagia Sophia has a TF rating of 8, Jerusalem should be scattered with 9's with a few 10's.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> i saw jerusalem by night and the max is 7. besides true faith is (presumably) gained gradually by people going to an area and treating it as holy place. or it being a place where lots of worship happens.<br /> <br /> im no history expert but i belive that hagia sophia at it's zenith propably had more people concentrating their worship there than the church of the holy sepulchre did.<br /> <br /> like wise if im not mistakes <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Masjid_al-Haram is the most important place in islam.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T15:38:02-08:00","id":420746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/410140-in-which-dark-age-books-do-i-find-a-chart-on-faith-rating-per-holy-building?p=420399#post420399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that pretty much anything can constitute a basis for True Faith, doesn't that render it effectively meaningless?<br /> <br /> Ex. (NOT REAL) I REALLY believe in the color pink. It colors (literally) everything I see (rose-colored glasses and all), what I do, where I go, what I wear, how I think about things. Any subject you bring up I can come up with some way it's impacted by pink and how it can be made better by pink... Vampires beware.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's meaningless in an absolute sense. Just like Paradigms are meaningless in Mage in an absolute sense. But at the end of the day the point is that just because you truly and utterly believe in something it matters. This is the key and power of True Faith. It matters because of the person who is willing to believe in something that may or may not be true and will do anything for this principle. Therefore it's probably the most important thing in the world <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T12:29:10-08:00","id":422118,"title":"","content":"that being said it is likely that,barring extreme examples most faiths do have <b>some</b> element of truth in them more or less.<br /> <br /> celestial chorus revised implies that there may be a benevolent(though id add a malevolent one too) power watching the universe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T01:19:50-08:00","id":422696,"title":"","content":"There are things in the Umbra that are equivalents of all Gods. Some of them exist because people care, others have latched onto human ideas to feed themselves and become more powerful. None of them are the source of True Faith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T02:08:01-08:00","id":422722,"title":"","content":"More or less the source of True Faith is within each of us. It is literally the power of one's Faith it doesn't come from a higher power, or a lower one, but from within. That is why it can be had by practitioners of several different religions even one's in direct opposition. True Faith on buildings and religious sites is the result of thousands upon thousands believing in them even if none of those believers themselves have actual True Faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T09:42:23-08:00","id":423054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/410140-in-which-dark-age-books-do-i-find-a-chart-on-faith-rating-per-holy-building?p=420582#post420582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> i saw jerusalem by night and the max is 7. besides true faith is (presumably) gained gradually by people going to an area and treating it as holy place. or it being a place where lots of worship happens.<br /> <br /> im no history expert but i belive that hagia sophia at it's zenith propably had more people concentrating their worship there than the church of the holy sepulchre did.<br /> <br /> like wise if im not mistakes <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Masjid_al-Haram is the most important place in islam.</span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Hagia Sophia may have been the central religious cite of the Byzantine Empire, it may have been the &quot;center of the world&quot; and the place where the Emperors were crowned, but no one in the Byzantine Empire would have considered it the center of the faith. A pilgrimage to Constantinople would never have been considered equal to one to Jerusalem. Likewise, the Vatican is REALLY important to Catholicism, but it's still not Jerusalem. Hence those Crusades. <br /> <br /> The Masjid al_Haram = the Church of the Holy Sepulchre = the Wailing Wall is a fairly close approximation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T09:48:39-08:00","id":423064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/410140-in-which-dark-age-books-do-i-find-a-chart-on-faith-rating-per-holy-building?p=422722#post422722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More or less the source of True Faith is within each of us. It is literally the power of one's Faith it doesn't come from a higher power, or a lower one, but from within. That is why it can be had by practitioners of several different religions even one's in direct opposition. True Faith on buildings and religious sites is the result of thousands upon thousands believing in them even if none of those believers themselves have actual True Faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, there is a cognitive disconnect here. If True Faith is internal, then it can't be vested in a place, no matter how many people project their devotion to it. Because that place is not internal. Particularly if the extreme case of none of the people projecting their devotion actually has True Faith. It's still not internal. Otherwise Fashion Week in Paris is replete with True Faith. Relativism isn't inherent in this. In the context of the game, there can be objectively real truths. All belief is not created equal. There many need to be some external force which the person or place with True Faith is syncing up to. <br /> <br /> In Dark Ages Vampire, if one could find the altar on which Abraham did not sacrifice Isaac or the place where Jesus told Satan to go screw, wouldn't those places have inherent True Faith? Even though they are completely and utterly lost as locations and would require masses of un-real devotion to be directed to a virtuality? And if that's the case, then there are a ton of places that have True Faith, but apparently don't exist....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T10:15:18-08:00","id":423079,"title":"","content":"What I mean is that True Faith is the power of the human soul as manifested through their faith when enough people have faith for something those small insignificant trickles do indeed form a river thus investing the place with True Faith rating of it's own. It's like each believer is leaving a small part of their own power into the place, the power originates within a human but as he invest it in a place it sticks, for most places it's too little to ever matter but when enough people invest in the same place it slowly starts to matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Dark Ages Vampire, if one could find the altar on which Abraham did not sacrifice Isaac or the place where Jesus told Satan to go screw, wouldn't those places have inherent True Faith? </div> </div> </div>It depends. Is Jesus a real figure in your game? And if so is he a incarnation of gods multifaceted being? If both of those are yes then sure the place can have True Faith but if Jesus was just another Mage showing of and trying to spread his personal Paradigm then no. And it can matter if this Jesus had True Faith of his own which he might have imprinted and invested into the place. All of these questions can also easily be answered as a no if Christianity is just a religion instead of truth in which case such a place no one knew of would not have a True Faith rating. Similar questions could be said about Abraham and Isaac.<br /> <br /> And then of course if you wish at your table True Faith could originate from some outer power whether divine or infernal but in general that does not seem to be the case according to most of what has been written of True Faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T11:16:50-08:00","id":423129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/410140-in-which-dark-age-books-do-i-find-a-chart-on-faith-rating-per-holy-building?p=423054#post423054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Hagia Sophia may have been the central religious cite of the Byzantine Empire, it may have been the &quot;center of the world&quot; and the place where the Emperors were crowned, but no one in the Byzantine Empire would have considered it the center of the faith. A pilgrimage to Constantinople would never have been considered equal to one to Jerusalem. Likewise, the Vatican is REALLY important to Catholicism, but it's still not Jerusalem. Hence those Crusades.<br /> <br /> The Masjid al_Haram = the Church of the Holy Sepulchre = the Wailing Wall is a fairly close approximation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> yes you are right . but as i understand it in order for a bulding to have true faith active worship needs to take place there. i don't think that just because it is considered very important would matter at all..<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T08:30:03-08:00","id":424176,"title":"","content":"Western Christianity was willing to fight war after war after war to keep access to the holy sites of Jerusalem. Islamic states were willing to do the same when their access was cut off to the same sites. <br /> <br /> I notice that there was no equivalent outpouring of violence when Mehmet took the Hagia Sophia. The relics Sophia brought back FROM JERUSALEM were the foundation of the sanctity of her church.<br /> <br /> I don't think that the fact that the Byzantine Emperors were crowned there, or that it was the seat of the highest cleric of the Eastern Orthodox Church brings it the same level of veneration as the sites in which the most important events of the religion actually occurred. Sites that were the objective of pilgrimage from all of the various branches of Christianity.<br /> <br /> And that's if you accept the idea that True Faith works like D&amp;D gods and is completely dependent on mass veneration. However, you can also argue that True Faith has just as much or even more to do with what actually happened in the spot in question. Perhaps the spot on the road to Damascus has True Faith 7 if anyone happened to stumble across it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T08:38:18-08:00","id":424182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/410140-in-which-dark-age-books-do-i-find-a-chart-on-faith-rating-per-holy-building?p=423079#post423079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends. Is Jesus a real figure in your game? And if so is he a incarnation of gods multifaceted being? If both of those are yes then sure the place can have True Faith but if Jesus was just another Mage showing of and trying to spread his personal Paradigm then no. And it can matter if this Jesus had True Faith of his own which he might have imprinted and invested into the place. All of these questions can also easily be answered as a no if Christianity is just a religion instead of truth in which case such a place no one knew of would not have a True Faith rating. Similar questions could be said about Abraham and Isaac.<br /> <br /> And then of course if you wish at your table True Faith could originate from some outer power whether divine or infernal but in general that does not seem to be the case according to most of what has been written of True Faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Caine? Is Lilith? There is a fundamental underpining of Abrahamic faith in some games (Vampire, Demon). And that is even stronger in DA. You can ignore it if you like in favor of a broader relativism. In which case, I BELIEVE in the power of pink, BEGONE SPAWN OF DARKNESS!&quot; (Meaning &quot;that which is not pink) Fishmalks unite! (or don't)! Because your derangement has a good chance to open you to the road to True Faith!<br /> <br /> The language on True Faith is equivocal. Sure you can have faith in God, the Devil or Odin and get True Faith, but it's hit and miss whether True Faith is pretty much just an advanced Code of Honor. And, to my mind, weakens it. <br /> <br /> &lt;Shrug&gt; It's totally up to you how you want to run and how your games work. <br /> <br /> In any case, it looks like that highest True Faith rating I can find for any building or area is 7. So the levels of True Faith in a place just don't get to the highest of high heights of faith. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T13:16:22-08:00","id":424418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is a fundamental underpining of Abrahamic faith in some games </div> </div> </div>I'd say that the Setites disagree and now with V20DA the new Laibon, I also doubt that the followers of Road of Einhenjar from Wolves of the Sea see it that way. Or the Lhiannan for that matter, the Ravnos have a bit different opinion as well. Or any Vampire that has been embraced before Abrahamic faiths were a thing like Ur-Shulgi for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because your derangement has a good chance to open you to the road to True Faith! </div> </div> </div>Believe it or not there is a fine line between deranged and a true believer, it may in some cases seem non.existent bu it is there, so I would doubt this would be possible. Also I strongly suspect that anyone really could believe in the power of pink so strongly that their souls resonate with it but hey it's your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1629,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","user":"Possessed","date":". 03-01-2015, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T15:07:46-08:00","id":424583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/410140-in-which-dark-age-books-do-i-find-a-chart-on-faith-rating-per-holy-building?p=424418#post424418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Believe it or not there is a fine line between deranged and a true believer, it may in some cases seem non.existent bu it is there, so I would doubt this would be possible. Also I strongly suspect that anyone really could believe in the power of pink so strongly that their souls resonate with it but hey it's your game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see, where in your definition, that line exists. There are many different mental disabilities that create absolute and total belief. If all the soul has to resonate with is itself, then they seem to meet your criteria for True Faith nigh perfectly. <br /> <br /> I latch on to the &quot;believe in the power of X so strongly that their souls resonate with it&quot; means that the souls in question aren't resonating with themselves, or, to be precise, the soul in question is not resonating with itself. That implies that the belief is something external to the believer. And it needs to be something other than pink or trees or marmalade or telephone polls or high school. It has to be something WITH a certain kind of resonance. Perhaps even in line with Mage-like resonance. Meaning it would need to be like some trans-pagan belief structure, or an underworld full of demons or a major theistic religion to whatever degree. And, furthermore, that is why places can even have True Faith. Not because the place believes in itself or that people believe in the place but because the place itself resonates with something ineffable and numinous. Not the color pink or trees, etc. but something immaterial but very real and definably external. And probably a few other things, because there are still quite a few things that would still fit inside that definition at which I would look askance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T20:21:12-08:00","id":424806,"title":"","content":"Well the if you insist that an external element is required it might even make your pink believer more likely than less actually as even pink likely has a spirit of it's own somewhere in the Umbra. So even in the case of it would need an external source, which it in my opinion after reading several descriptors of True Faith doesn't, it still requires one to hold on to the line between belief and deranged. Why did I bring up the line between the two? Because there are plenty of people who are nuts and have gone over the line so to speak towards one religions or another yet despite having similar amount of belief in something doesn't make them have True Faith like someone who isn't mad believing in the very same religion. If fanaticism was all that was required True Faith would be much more common, scarily so in fact.<br /> <br /> Demon the Fallen explains this in character in the core book if I remember correctly as it speaks about why Demons can't generate Faith but humans can. The difference is that the Demon knows there is a God while a human doesn't and must rely on belief alone, on faith alone that is to say to have faith one needs to have that uncertainty or it isn't truly faith anymore. If you are deranged in a manner that you know that pink is the universal truth that can drive away evil, everything not pink, you cannot have true faith and thus you also cannot have True Faith. Madness brought, and fanaticism brought, belief is based on the deranged one knowing something for a fact hence they cannot have that kind of belief in it. In WoD such fine lines matter. Madness is certain from the perspective of the mad one while one truly devout always has that uncertainty in it that they acknowledge it all as a matter of faith not knowledge.<br /> <br /> It's early, inhumanly so, so I might have some difficulty expressing myself but hopefully you get the point. Still like I've also hopefully made clear YMMV and at your table things are as you wish they are but this is how I have come to understand True Faith through the various texts about it throughout the books.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, and speaking of Demon. Which you brought up as an example of a line where Abrahamic Faiths are basically correct, or if not quite correct close enough as it were. In Demon any active use of Faith by humans, which would include True Faith even though that particular line is the only line where no such Merit made an appearance, is not about tapping the power of some external being, like God, but tapping into the inherent divinity of the human soul. According to Demon each human has a divine spark within that they can tap for power, and some do more so than others Mages being most in touch with this spark, and which could grow from that spark into a conflagration rising humanity into godhood themselves. So the game line that has Abrahamic faiths as it's strongest underpinning is the one that makes it clearest that the power of human Faith is inherent not external. So there is that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1629,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","user":"Possessed","date":". 03-01-2015, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T09:15:47-08:00","id":425290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/410140-in-which-dark-age-books-do-i-find-a-chart-on-faith-rating-per-holy-building?p=424806#post424806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the if you insist that an external element is required it might even make your pink believer more likely than less actually as even pink likely has a spirit of it's own somewhere in the Umbra. So even in the case of it would need an external source, which it in my opinion after reading several descriptors of True Faith doesn't, it still requires one to hold on to the line between belief and deranged. Why did I bring up the line between the two? Because there are plenty of people who are nuts and have gone over the line so to speak towards one religions or another yet despite having similar amount of belief in something doesn't make them have True Faith like someone who isn't mad believing in the very same religion. If fanaticism was all that was required True Faith would be much more common, scarily so in fact.<br /> <br /> Demon the Fallen explains this in character in the core book if I remember correctly as it speaks about why Demons can't generate Faith but humans can. The difference is that the Demon knows there is a God while a human doesn't and must rely on belief alone, on faith alone that is to say to have faith one needs to have that uncertainty or it isn't truly faith anymore. If you are deranged in a manner that you know that pink is the universal truth that can drive away evil, everything not pink, you cannot have true faith and thus you also cannot have True Faith. Madness brought, and fanaticism brought, belief is based on the deranged one knowing something for a fact hence they cannot have that kind of belief in it. In WoD such fine lines matter. Madness is certain from the perspective of the mad one while one truly devout always has that uncertainty in it that they acknowledge it all as a matter of faith not knowledge.<br /> <br /> It's early, inhumanly so, so I might have some difficulty expressing myself but hopefully you get the point. Still like I've also hopefully made clear YMMV and at your table things are as you wish they are but this is how I have come to understand True Faith through the various texts about it throughout the books.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, and speaking of Demon. Which you brought up as an example of a line where Abrahamic Faiths are basically correct, or if not quite correct close enough as it were. In Demon any active use of Faith by humans, which would include True Faith even though that particular line is the only line where no such Merit made an appearance, is not about tapping the power of some external being, like God, but tapping into the inherent divinity of the human soul. According to Demon each human has a divine spark within that they can tap for power, and some do more so than others Mages being most in touch with this spark, and which could grow from that spark into a conflagration rising humanity into godhood themselves. So the game line that has Abrahamic faiths as it's strongest underpinning is the one that makes it clearest that the power of human Faith is inherent not external. So there is that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would still want something more than a deeply held completely personal belief. And more than an attachment to something like a spirit. I don't think a character's personal belief in PINK should be enough to warrant a dot of True Faith.<br /> <br /> &quot;Stop trying to anthropomorphize PINK! I don't believe in some spirit of Pink, I believe in true Pink, the color like no other! Come, let me demonstrate the truth of Pink. Pink is more true, more real than any God worshipped in a church. Pink is REAL. Here, take a look at this &lt;random pink object&gt;. See? That is PINK. Now do you understand? No? Then you are looking without SEEING the grandeur and wonder of Pink&quot;<br /> <br /> That doesn't work for me. <br /> <br /> I think one of the underlying issues that ends up in a minefield for any discussion of True Faith is the various different versions that populate the WoD. I have seen the same discussion of the nature of Faith vs. True Faith used for the Celestial Chorus. They don't/can't have faith b/c they KNOW it's real and faith has to be unreasoning, blind and unproved. Which opens up a whole set of new cans full of many different species of worms... Many of the descriptions of True Faith make is seem so intrinsically personal that there doesn't seem to be a logical way to argue that places can have it. Others are very simplistic. True Faith is a representation that sometimes it's cool to have vampires not be able to walk into church and sometimes it's cool to have them flinch or flee from a cross, because those things happen in a lot of the source material and 'base code&quot; for part of the perception of what vampires ARE. But it doesn't have to go much past that. Faith is similar, but different in Demon than DA Inquisitor. Darkening Skies takes some of the True Faith info set up for vampires in Jerusalem and applied it to Mages, DA Mages no less and how that affects mage magic in a manner that somewhat tracks the Dominion from Ars Magica with the caveat that religion isn't just inherent anit-magic but a different kind of magic and that the two can interfere with each other. <br /> <br /> Discussion about True Faith can end up with one party grabbing one part of the web of inter-related, sometimes harmonious, sometimes contradictory definitions of True Faith and another person taking ahold of it somewhere else and both sides trying to yank it into some semblance of order based on the first principles they are operating from. A lot of it has to be put down to where the various games are coming from... the whole &quot;these are different systems that seem like they're in the same world, but may not be, probably aren't, shouldn't be&quot; or whatever. True Faith seems like it can be all things to all people, but, specifically it is what you need it to be now...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}